meta {
  name: Create Request - duplicate
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{apiUrl}}/requests
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{idToken2}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 409
  res.body.success: eq false
  res.body.error.code: eq DUPLICATE_REQUEST
}

docs {
  Implemented (D3). Run **Create Request** first (as the player), then this, as the
  **same player** -- a duplicate only exists if it's the same `PK`+`SK`
  (`SESSION#<id>` / `REQUEST#USER#<playerId>`), so this must use `{{idToken2}}`, not the
  host's token.

  `request.repository.ts`'s `create()` catches `ConditionalCheckFailedException` from the
  `attribute_not_exists(PK) OR #s = :withdrawn` write and throws `DuplicateRequestError` ->
  409. The `OR` half is Phase 3.5: a `WITHDRAWN` request's item can be overwritten by a
  fresh join (see **Host Decisions / Create Request - rejoin after withdraw**), so this
  test specifically needs the request to still be *live* (`PENDING` here) for the
  duplicate guard to actually fire.
}
